      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-223208",
      ":question/problem": "An object vibrates vertically. The distance between the object and its central position, in millimeters, can be modeled by a function of the form $D(t) = A\\sin (Bt)$, where $A$ and $B$ are constants and $t$ is the time (in seconds). Assume that the positive direction is upward.\n\nIt is observed that when $t = 0.1$, the object is at its maximum height, $5$ millimeters above its central position. Then, after $0.3$ seconds, the object reaches its minimum height of $5$ millimeters below its central position.\n\nWhich of the following could be the function $D(t)$?"
    },
