      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-223212",
      ":question/problem": "A heart pumps blood in and out of its chambers. The volume of blood in the heart, in milliliters, can be modeled by a function of the form $V(t) = 35\\cos (Bt) + C$, where $B$ and $C$ are constants and $t$ is the time (in seconds).\n\nIt is observed that when $t = 0$, the heart contains its maximum volume of blood, $140$ milliliters. Then, after $1.5$ seconds, the heart contains its minimum volume of blood.\n\nWhich of the following could be the function $V(t)$?"
